# .spool/coverage.req

feature: COVERAGE

requirements:

  - id: COVERAGE-1
    title: Coverage Report
    description: >
      The get_coverage_report tool must return Spool's coverage report
      for the project, as JSON by default or as text or markdown.
    status: active
    deciders:
      - Matt Ames
    consulted: []
    date: 2026-11-12
    rationale: >
      An agent checking a project's traceability wants the same report
      a developer gets from the spool command, not a second rendering
      of it that can drift. The tool passes Spool's own formatters
      through: JSON as a structured object an agent can read without
      parsing text, and text or markdown as Spool prints them. The
      coverage tools and their tests shipped in v1 without this spec;
      it is written from what they do.
    superseded_by:
    out_of_scope:
      - Coverage for listed IDs (spool --ids)
      - Reporting on part of a project
    acceptance_criteria:

      - id: COVERAGE-1-1
        title: JSON by Default
        description: >
          Given a project and no format, or format json,
          when get_coverage_report is invoked,
          then the result has format "json" and a report object equal
          to the JSON report Spool produces for that project.

      - id: COVERAGE-1-2
        title: Text Format
        description: >
          Given format text,
          when get_coverage_report is invoked,
          then the result has format "text" and text holding Spool's
          text report for the project exactly.

      - id: COVERAGE-1-3
        title: Markdown Format
        description: >
          Given format markdown,
          when get_coverage_report is invoked,
          then the result has format "markdown" and text holding
          Spool's markdown report for the project exactly.

      - id: COVERAGE-1-4
        title: Unknown Format Rejected
        description: >
          Given any other format,
          when get_coverage_report is invoked,
          then the response is an error with category
          "invalid_arguments" and a message naming json, text and
          markdown.

  - id: COVERAGE-2
    title: Untested AC Listing
    description: >
      The list_untested_acs tool must list the project's active ACs
      that have no linked test, optionally narrowed to one feature.
    status: active
    deciders:
      - Matt Ames
    consulted: []
    date: 2026-11-12
    rationale: >
      This is the agent's to-do list: what it can work through without
      reading the whole report. An AC counts when Spool counts it, so
      the list follows Spool's per-item status (SPEC-4-5 in Spool):
      draft and deprecated ACs, and every AC of a superseded
      requirement, are left out, because they aren't expected to have
      tests. Each entry carries the AC's text so the agent can act on
      it without a lookup.
    superseded_by:
    out_of_scope:
      - Untested invariants
      - Ordering of the list
      - Filtering by requirement or status
    acceptance_criteria:

      - id: COVERAGE-2-1
        title: Untested Active AC Listed
        description: >
          Given an active AC with no linked test, and an active AC
          with one,
          when list_untested_acs is invoked,
          then the untested list includes the first with its id,
          title, description, requirement_id and feature, and doesn't
          include the second.

      - id: COVERAGE-2-2
        title: Non-Active ACs Excluded
        description: >
          Given untested ACs that are draft or deprecated, or that
          belong to a superseded requirement,
          when list_untested_acs is invoked,
          then none of them is in the untested list.

      - id: COVERAGE-2-3
        title: Feature Filter Applied
        description: >
          Given untested ACs in more than one feature and a feature
          argument,
          when list_untested_acs is invoked,
          then the untested list holds only that feature's untested
          ACs.

  - id: COVERAGE-3
    title: Orphaned Annotation Listing
    description: >
      The list_orphaned_annotations tool must list the test annotations
      that name a Spool ID no .req file defines.
    status: active
    deciders:
      - Matt Ames
    consulted: []
    date: 2026-11-12
    rationale: >
      An orphaned annotation is a broken link: a typo, a deleted
      requirement, or a test written ahead of its spec. Giving the file
      and line lets an agent go straight to it.
    superseded_by:
    out_of_scope:
      - Suggesting the ID an orphan was meant to be
    acceptance_criteria:

      - id: COVERAGE-3-1
        title: Orphan Reported
        description: >
          Given a test annotated with an ID that no .req file defines,
          when list_orphaned_annotations is invoked,
          then the orphaned list holds an entry with that ID, the test
          file's path and the annotation's line.

      - id: COVERAGE-3-2
        title: Known ID Not Reported
        description: >
          Given a test annotated with an ID that a .req file defines,
          when list_orphaned_annotations is invoked,
          then that annotation is not in the orphaned list.

      - id: COVERAGE-3-3
        title: Empty Orphaned List
        description: >
          Given a project with no orphaned annotations,
          when list_orphaned_annotations is invoked,
          then the result is a success whose orphaned list is empty,
          not null.

  - id: COVERAGE-4
    title: Validation Error Listing
    description: >
      The list_validation_errors tool must list the errors Spool finds
      when it indexes the project's .req files.
    status: active
    deciders:
      - Matt Ames
    consulted: []
    date: 2026-11-12
    rationale: >
      Duplicate IDs and IDs that don't match their file's feature make
      the traceability graph ambiguous, and Spool reports them as index
      errors rather than failing. Listing them lets an agent fix the
      specs before trusting anything else the tools return.
    superseded_by:
    out_of_scope:
      - Parse warnings for malformed .req files (PROJECT-3)
      - Structured fields beyond the message
    acceptance_criteria:

      - id: COVERAGE-4-1
        title: Duplicate Requirement ID
        description: >
          Given two .req files that both define the same requirement
          ID,
          when list_validation_errors is invoked,
          then the errors list has a message naming that ID as a
          duplicate.

      - id: COVERAGE-4-2
        title: Duplicate AC ID
        description: >
          Given two requirements that both define the same AC ID,
          when list_validation_errors is invoked,
          then the errors list has a message naming that ID as a
          duplicate.

      - id: COVERAGE-4-3
        title: Prefix Mismatch
        description: >
          Given a .req file whose feature doesn't match the prefix of
          a requirement ID in it,
          when list_validation_errors is invoked,
          then the errors list has a message naming that ID.

      - id: COVERAGE-4-4
        title: Clean Project
        description: >
          Given a project with no duplicate IDs or prefix mismatches,
          when list_validation_errors is invoked,
          then the result is a success whose errors list is empty, not
          null.
